'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  ch14-pasm-scope.spin2
''   Purpose....  A SCOPE window fed from a PASM cog launched with
''                coginit, not from Spin2
''   Manual.....  P2 Debug Window Manual
''   Version....  v1.1.3 (2026-08-18)
''   Appears in.  Chapter 14: Multiple Windows and PASM Debugging --
''                Debugging from PASM
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Jun 2026
''   Updated....  Aug 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. Everything below
''   this header is byte-identical to the listing printed there --
''   what you read in the manual is what builds here.
''
'' ===========================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000

PUB main()
  coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @blink, 0)  ' launch the PASM program in its own cog
  repeat                                  ' keep the Spin2 cog alive

DAT
              org
blink
              debug(`SCOPE Wave SIZE 400 200)  ' create with config only
              debug(`Wave 'Ramp' 0 255)     ' channel-def as a separate feed
.loop
              add       value, #4        ' advance a software ramp
              and       value, #$FF
              ' feed the window with the register's value
              debug(`Wave `(value))
              waitx     ##2_000_000
              jmp       #.loop

value         long      0

